{"schema":1,"id":"lantern","title":"How can a still skip the frames before it?","lang":"en","sources":["https://github.com/ivarvong/lantern","https://github.com/ivarvong/lantern/blob/2c7bad5/src/scene.ts","https://github.com/adewale/rayner/blob/main/src/scene.ts","https://github.com/adewale/rayner/blob/main/src/animation.ts"],"settings":[{"id":"motion","label":"The dot moves by","default":"nudge","options":[{"value":"blend","label":"Blending fixed endpoints"},{"value":"nudge","label":"A nudge each frame"}]}],"answer":"A still re-runs the scene on the same fixed clock and, unless the scene has updaters or is playing a Succession, skips computing the frames before t, so it matches playback whenever each frame depends on the time alone, and can miss when a frame depends on how many frames ran before it","checks":[{"question":"In the nudge version, the fade-in is stretched from 0.5 s to 1 s, so the move runs from t = 1 s to 2 s and the scene has 60 frames. Does the still at t = 1 s now match playback, and which is the first frame whose still differs?","answer":"The still at t = 1 s matches: frame 30 is now the last frame of the fade, and neither run has nudged the dot yet. The first frame that differs is 32. Frame 31 opens the move, and the seek and playback have each made one nudge there; by frame 32 playback has made two and the seek still one."},{"question":"Another version moves the dot by the change in time since the last frame it computed: x += distance × (α − α at the last frame). Does its still at t = 1 s match playback?","answer":"Yes. begin() computes α = 0, the skipped frames are never computed, and the frame at t = 1 s adds the whole change from 0 to 0.5 in one go, so the dot is halfway, as in playback. Keeping state is allowed, as long as the frame comes out the same however many frames ran before it."}],"cases":[{"values":{"motion":"blend"},"name":"The dot moves by: Blending fixed endpoints","duration":135.833,"paper":"#f7f5ef","steps":[{"step":"played","title":"Played, the dot is halfway at t = 1.00 s","line":"a still at t = 1 s skips computing frames 1–29. Where is its dot?","caption":"A direct link opens a later picture without playing the earlier steps. Here a box fades in, then a dot moves along a track. Rayner’s animate.moveTo moves the dot by blending its start and end. Playback has the dot halfway at t = 1 s. The still re-runs the scene but only counts the earlier frames. Where will its dot be?","start":0,"end":22.9,"hold":1.3,"state":{},"changed":{},"picture":"Left: the tiny scene played: frame 30, t = 1.00 s, the dot halfway along its track, fingerprint 65f5f588. Right: an empty frame marked with a question mark, seeked: frames 1–29 only counted.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│           played: frame 30, t = 1.00 s              seeked: frames 1–29 only counted\n│       ┌───────────────────────────────────┐       ┌───────────────────────────────────┐\n│       │       ┌─────────────┐             │       │                                   │\n│       │       │             │             │       │                                   │\n│       │       │             │             │       │                                   │\n│       │       │             │             │       │                                   │\n│       │       └─────────────┘             │       │                 ?                 │\n│       │                                   │       │                                   │\n│       │                                   │       │                                   │\n│       │    ─────────────●───────────────  │       │                                   │\n│       │                                   │       │                                   │\n│       └───────────────────────────────────┘       └───────────────────────────────────┘\n│             svg 65f5f588 · 1458 chars\n│\n│\n│\n│"},{"step":"seek","title":"The still matches: the same SVG, fingerprint 65f5f588","line":"Blending works the dot out from the time alone.","caption":"The pictures match because animate.moveTo calculates position from elapsed time and fixed endpoints. It does not need the earlier dot positions. A still re-runs the scene on the same fixed clock and, unless the scene has updaters or is playing a Succession, skips computing the frames before t, so it matches playback whenever each frame depends on the time alone, and can miss when a frame depends on how many frames ran before it.","start":22.9,"end":50.667,"hold":25.6,"state":{"seek":{"motion":"blend","match":true,"played":"65f5f588","seeked":"65f5f588","playedMoves":0,"seekedMoves":0}},"changed":{"seek":{"after":{"motion":"blend","match":true,"played":"65f5f588","seeked":"65f5f588","playedMoves":0,"seekedMoves":0}}},"picture":"Two frames of the tiny scene at t = 1.00 s, played and seeked, both with the dot halfway and the fingerprint 65f5f588.; 1 label.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│           played: frame 30, t = 1.00 s              seeked: frames 1–29 only counted\n│       ┌───────────────────────────────────┐       ┌───────────────────────────────────┐\n│       │       ┌─────────────┐             │       │      ┌─────────────┐              │\n│       │       │             │             │       │      │             │              │\n│       │       │             │             │       │      │             │              │\n│       │       │             │             │       │      │             │              │\n│       │       └─────────────┘             │   =   │      └─────────────┘              │\n│       │                                   │       │                                   │\n│       │                                   │       │                                   │\n│       │    ─────────────●───────────────  │       │   ──────────────●──────────────   │\n│       │                                   │       │                                   │\n│       └───────────────────────────────────┘       └───────────────────────────────────┘\n│             svg 65f5f588 · 1458 chars                   svg 65f5f588 · 1458 chars\n│\n│\n│\n│"},{"step":"clock","title":"Frame 30 is t = 1.00 s in every run","line":"Scene time is the frame number × 1/30 s, however fast the frames are taken.","caption":"The receiver of a frame is called a sink. A browser sink waits between frames; a trace sink can take them immediately. That changes how fast the output arrives, not the scene’s clock: both reach t = 1 s at frame 30. The target time therefore identifies the same frame even when earlier pictures are skipped.","start":50.667,"end":71.667,"hold":55.6,"state":{"seek":{"motion":"blend","match":true,"played":"65f5f588","seeked":"65f5f588","playedMoves":0,"seekedMoves":0},"walks":[{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Browser","edge":"edge:Clock->Browser#0"},{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Trace","edge":"edge:Clock->Trace#0"}],"frameAtSeek":30},"changed":{"walks":{"after":[{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Browser","edge":"edge:Clock->Browser#0"},{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Trace","edge":"edge:Clock->Trace#0"}]},"frameAtSeek":{"after":30}},"picture":"Flowchart: 6 nodes, 5 links; 12 labels. Travelled: Fixed dt loop → Browser sink; Fixed dt loop → State trace.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│                  ▌\n│                  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│                  ────────────────────────────────┌──────────┐───────────────\n│                  ────────────────────────────┌───│──────────│───────────────\n│                  ▌                           │   └──────────┘\n│                  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│                  ────────────────────────────│───│──────────────────────────\n│                  ────────────────────────────│───┌────────┐─────────────────\n│                  ────────────────────────────└───│────────│─────────────────\n│                  ────────────────────────────────└────────┘─────────────────\n│                  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│                  ▌\n│\n│\n│                          ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│   scene time (ms)         0      33      67      100    133     167     200     233     267\n│\n│\n│   browser sink, wall clock●       ●       ●       ●      ●       ●       ●       ●       ●\n│\n│   trace sink, wall clock  ● ● ●● ● ●● ● ●\n│\n│"},{"step":"objects","title":"A frame is the shapes on stage, as the playing animations left them","line":"Once the still reaches frame 30, the playing animation decides where the dot is.","caption":"A Scene owns the shapes and text, called mobjects, and its animations change them. Rayner’s sinks only read the frame. The output cannot reconstruct missing nudges: the dot’s position must already be right when the animation hands over that frame.","start":71.667,"end":86.667,"hold":78.567,"state":{"seek":{"motion":"blend","match":true,"played":"65f5f588","seeked":"65f5f588","playedMoves":0,"seekedMoves":0},"walks":[{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Browser","edge":"edge:Clock->Browser#0"},{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Trace","edge":"edge:Clock->Trace#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Mobject","edge":"rel:Scene->Mobject#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Animation","edge":"rel:Scene->Animation#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Sink","edge":"rel:Scene->Sink#0"}],"frameAtSeek":30},"changed":{"walks":{"before":[{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Browser","edge":"edge:Clock->Browser#0"},{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Trace","edge":"edge:Clock->Trace#0"}],"after":[{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Browser","edge":"edge:Clock->Browser#0"},{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Trace","edge":"edge:Clock->Trace#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Mobject","edge":"rel:Scene->Mobject#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Animation","edge":"rel:Scene->Animation#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Sink","edge":"rel:Scene->Sink#0"}]}},"picture":"Class diagram: 4 classes, 3 relationships; Beside Sink: it reads each frame and changes nothing. Travelled: Scene → Mobject: owns; Scene → Animation: plays; Scene → Sink: emits.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│     ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│     │                                                    │\n│     ───────────────────────────────────┌─────────────┐────\n│     ───────────────────────────────────│─────────────│────\n│     │                 ┌─────────────────────────────── reads each frame; changes nothing\n│     ──────────────────│───────────────────────────────────\n│     ──────────────────│────────────────└─────────────┘────\n│     ──────────────────│────────────────│──────────────────\n│     │                 │                ┌─────────────┐   │\n│     ──────────────────│────────────────│─────────────│────\n│     ──────────────────│─────┌────┐────────────────────────\n│     │                 │─────│────│─────│──────       │   │\n│     ──────────────────│─────└────┘─────│─────────────│────\n│     ────┌─────────────┐───────────────────────────────────\n│     │   │    ─────    │                └─────────────┘   │\n│     ───────────────────────────────────┘──────────────────\n│     ────│─────────────│────────────────┌─────────────┐────\n│     │   │──────       │     ┌────┐     │    ───────  │   │\n│     ────│─────────────│─────│────│────────────────────────\n│     ────└─────────────┘─────└────┘─────│─────────────│────\n│     │                                  └─────────────┘   │\n│     ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│     └────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"step":"begin","title":"An animation fixes its endpoints when it begins","line":"At t = 1 s the blend is halfway, however many frames ran before.","caption":"begin() copies the starting object. Each frame blends that copy with a fixed end by an amount set only by how far through its run time the animation is. Halfway through the duration therefore means halfway between the endpoints. In contrast, dot.shift(step) adds to the position accumulated by earlier frames.","start":86.667,"end":105.433,"hold":89.9,"state":{"seek":{"motion":"blend","match":true,"played":"65f5f588","seeked":"65f5f588","playedMoves":0,"seekedMoves":0},"walks":[{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Browser","edge":"edge:Clock->Browser#0"},{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Trace","edge":"edge:Clock->Trace#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Mobject","edge":"rel:Scene->Mobject#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Animation","edge":"rel:Scene->Animation#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Sink","edge":"rel:Scene->Sink#0"}],"frameAtSeek":30},"changed":{},"picture":"Class diagram: 4 classes, 3 relationships; Code, 9 lines. Note: “endpoints fixed at begin()” beside Animation interpolate(). New in this step: Code, 9 lines.","drawing":"      ┌───────┐       │                   │     │\n──────│───────│───────└──────────────────────────\n      └───────┘       ││────────          │     │\n──────────────────────││──────────────────│──────\n                      └───────────────────┘     │\n───────────────────────│─────────────────────────\n                       │                        │\n──────────────────────┌───────────────────┐──────\n                      ││    ─────────     │     │\n──────┌───────┐───────└──────────────────────────\n──────│───────│───────││───────           │   ┌─────────────────────────────┐\n──────│───────│───────││──────────────────│───│──                           │\n      └───────┘       ││──────            │   │ │// src/animation.ts        │\n──────────────────────│───────────────────────│──begin():                   │\n                      └───────────────────┘   │ │  start = mobject.copy()   │\n───────────────────────┘──────────────────────│──each frame:                │\n                       │                      │ │  blend(start, end,        │\n──────────────────────┌───────────────────┐───│──                           │\n                      │    ───────────    │   │ │    rateFunc(t / runTime)) │\n──────┌───────┐───────│────────────────────   │ │                           │\n──────│───────│───────└───────────────────────│──// the nudge, each frame:  │\n      └───────┘       │ ───────────────   │   │ │  dot.shift(step)          │\n──────────────────────└───────────────────┘───│──                           │\n                    ┌────────────────────────┐└─────────────────────────────┘\n───────────────────endpoints fixed at begin()│───\n────────────────────└────────────────────────┘──┘\n"},{"step":"check","title":"Seeked frame by frame: 45 of 45 match with blending, 16 with the nudge","line":"rayner check fails a page on the first seeked frame that differs from playback.","caption":"The strips compare all 45 frames of this tiny scene with independently seeked stills. Blending agrees throughout; the nudge first differs at frame 17. rayner check samples less: in every step of every case it seeks one frame midway and one just before the step ends. A mismatch fails the check, but agreement at those two times does not prove every possible time. An updater follows a different path: in a scene with updaters, a still computes every frame before t.","start":105.433,"end":135.833,"hold":107.133,"state":{"seek":{"motion":"blend","match":true,"played":"65f5f588","seeked":"65f5f588","playedMoves":0,"seekedMoves":0},"walks":[{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Browser","edge":"edge:Clock->Browser#0"},{"step":"clock","from":"Clock","to":"Trace","edge":"edge:Clock->Trace#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Mobject","edge":"rel:Scene->Mobject#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Animation","edge":"rel:Scene->Animation#0"},{"step":"objects","from":"Scene","to":"Sink","edge":"rel:Scene->Sink#0"}],"frameAtSeek":30,"check":{"frames":45,"matched":{"blend":45,"nudge":16}}},"changed":{"check":{"after":{"frames":45,"matched":{"blend":45,"nudge":16}}}},"picture":"Two rows of 45 cells, one per frame of the tiny scene, each comparing the seeked frame with the played one. Blending: all 45 match. A nudge each frame: frames 1 to 16 match, frames 17 to 45 differ. A line marks frame 30, the still at t = 1.00 s.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                                               the still at t = 1.00 s\n│                                                          ┌┐\n│                                                          ││\n│          Blending fixed endpoints: 45 of 45 match        ││\n│           ───────────────────────────────────────────────││────────────────────────\n│                                                          ││\n│                                                          ││\n│                                                          ││\n│          A nudge each frame: 16 of 45 match              ││\n│           ───────────────────────────────────────────────││────────────────────────\n│                                                          ││\n│                                                          └┘\n│    frame  1                     15                      30                      45\n│\n│                    filled: seeked frame = played frame · hollow: different\n│\n│\n│\n│"}]},{"values":{"motion":"nudge"},"name":"The dot moves by: A nudge each frame","duration":144.467,"paper":"#f7f5ef","steps":[{"step":"played"